# Linear improvement ticket

## How to use

Create or update an issue with `save_issue`. Put this body in `description`. An improvement changes behavior that already exists. Use the feature template for a new capability.

- `priority`: `1` Urgent, `2` High, `3` Medium, or `4` Low. Use `3` unless the user states otherwise.
- `addLabels`: an existing label from `list_issue_labels`.
- `blockedBy` and `relatedTo`: only issues the user names.
- `project`: the epic's project name, id, or `P-ENG-123` when the improvement belongs to one.
- `estimate`: set only when the user supplies a number.

Write a title that names the current behavior and the change. Delete any section below that does not apply.

## Body

```markdown
## Summary

[What exists today, what should change, and why.]

## Requirements

- [Testable change.]
- [Behavior that must stay the same.]

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] [The changed outcome.]
- [ ] [An existing behavior that still holds.]
- [ ] [Edge case, when the change has one.]

## Technical notes

[Constraints or modules to touch. Omit when there are none.]

## Testing

- [ ] Automated tests cover the changed behavior.
- [ ] Manual check: [the user flow to try.]

## Out of scope

- [Change this issue does not include.]
```
